{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/278997-homogenous-memory-vs-never-here","id":278997,"title":"Homogenous memory vs Never Here","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-12T13:35:58-07:00","id":278997,"title":"Homogenous memory vs Never Here","content":"I have an issue regarding these two embeds from the mundane category. Namely that one of them seems to be redundant.<br /> Homogenous memory seems to be able to do everything that Never Here can do - erase the demon from the memory of onlookers - as well as a host of more versatile changes without any apparent drawbacks. What's more Never Here has a weakness as an affected character has a chance of remembering the demons actions if he sees him again wheras this isn't mentionned at all in the text of Homogenous memory. The only apparent negative trait to HM is that supernatural investigation can reveal the truth without difficultty, which should probably be the case for Never Here too.<br /> <br /> Has anyone else noticed this inconsistency? Am I missing something in the descriptions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4066-xavier","name":"Xavier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T04:54:18-07:00","id":283717,"title":"","content":"Well from what I can see homogenous memory deals with what happened in a scene, it changes he was pushed to he jumped. It does not take the demon out the scene and do not change what happened just how people think it has happened. Never here just takes you out the scene.<br /> Also if you was flying around in demon form you need to come up with a good cover story, it was a bird, it was a plane is up to the GM to decide if \u201cthe cover story isn't completely absurd or impossible&quot;. A GM might say that a plane could not fly that low or how could it be inside. Even then the story can have holes that means that someone who has some smarts could put 2 and 2 together and figure the story you made up has holes.<br /> <br /> Homogenous memory does not stop mind reading or things like spirt touch, the best you have is if you get 5 successes and give a penalty equal to your Primum to mind reading type people.<br /> <br /> Never here does not need a good story or context. You just where never there. I had a player grill a mortal for info and then use never here to make it seem it could read the dude's mind. With homogenous memory you can not take away the memory of you but what you did from hitting the guy or saving his life. But you would have had to have interacted in some way, &quot;the demon's power is affecting the event and how it is perceived to any witness&quot;. An event still happened just you made it seem different.<br /> Never here gives you no sign of being there in the person's mind, with 5 successes &quot;some form of magical memory recovery would be necessary to allow the target to remember.&quot;<br /> <br /> In demon I feel the strongest powers are things like Left/Right or Play On Words. The powers where you have to think to make the most of them. Once you start to think though mistakes can happen. They are not powers that you can just use when ever you need. Powers like never here are quick and easy. If you was a demon in real life how much time would you have when an angel is on your tale? Would you waste time trying to come up with a good cover story that will get him to look else where or just never be in the scene?<br /> <br /> Then you have all the time you need to use homogenous memory for if you bump into that angel again<br /> <br /> Sorry for rambling","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4090-mental-state","name":"Mental-State","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}